optimization_strategy.modification_plan:
SMEM BUDGET CHECK (mandatory): tile is 32x33 floats = 4224 B per block, buffers=1, vs 227 KB/block limit on H100 -> passes by 50x; occupancy limit from smem is >32 blocks/SM, so no gate violation.

1. In _SRC add the generic kernel (exact index math):
```
__global__ void transpose_cs_kernel(const float* __restrict__ src,
                                    float* __restrict__ dst,
                                    int C, int S) {
  __shared__ float tile[32][33];
  const int n = blockIdx.z;
  const int p0 = blockIdx.x * 32, c0 = blockIdx.y * 32;
  const int tx = threadIdx.x, ty = threadIdx.y;   // blockDim=(32,8)
  const long long sbase = (long long)n * C * S;
  #pragma unroll
  for (int k = 0; k < 32; k += 8) {
    int c = c0 + ty + k, p = p0 + tx;
    if (c < C && p < S) tile[ty + k][tx] = src[sbase + (long long)c * S + p];
  }
  __syncthreads();
  const long long dbase = (long long)n * S * C;
  #pragma unroll
  for (int k = 0; k < 32; k += 8) {
    int c = c0 + tx, p = p0 + ty + k;
    if (c < C && p < S) dst[dbase + (long long)p * C + c] = tile[tx][ty + k];
  }
}
```
Reads: a warp fetches 32 consecutive p (128B). Writes: a warp writes 32 consecutive c (128B). smem read stride 33 -> bank-conflict free.

2. Add launcher `torch::Tensor to_nhwc(torch::Tensor t)`: TORCH_CHECK float32 + t.dim()==4 + t.is_contiguous(); `auto out = at::empty(t.sizes(), t.options().memory_format(at::MemoryFormat::ChannelsLast));` N=size(0), C=size(1), S=size(2)*size(3); `dim3 grid((S+31)/32, (C+31)/32, N); transpose_cs_kernel<<<grid, dim3(32,8), 0, stream>>>(t.data_ptr<float>(), out.data_ptr<float>(), C, S);` + C10_CUDA_KERNEL_LAUNCH_CHECK. This same launcher serves the weights: for (O,I,3,3) it is N=O, C=I=256, S=9, and channels_last strides (I*9,1,3I,I) give dst offset o*2304+s*256+i, exactly what the kernel writes. Declare it in _CPP and add "to_nhwc" to the functions list.

3. In ModelNew.forward replace
   `xl = x.contiguous(memory_format=torch.channels_last)` -> `xl = _ext.to_nhwc(x) if x.is_contiguous() else x.contiguous(memory_format=torch.channels_last)`
   and identically for `w1 = ...conv1_weight...`, `w2 = ...conv2_weight...`. Keep the existing fallback branch untouched, and keep reading the residual from `xl` in gn_silu_res_nhwc so the round-6 nhwc_output_layout_elimination mechanism stays fully operational (no new transpose, launch count per forward unchanged at 3 layout kernels).

4. Compile; validate torch.allclose vs the reference on all four shapes, especially 1x256x131x131 (S=17161, not a multiple of 32) to exercise the p<S tail guard, and 2x256x64x64. THIS IS THE MILESTONE — stop here if turns run low.

